window.__ykCourses = window.__ykCourses || {};
window.__ykCourses.N3 = {"level":"N3","units":[{"n":1,"ja":"時・タイミング","en":"Time and timing","days":[{"title":"〜たびに・〜ごとに","grammar":{"points":[{"id":"n3u01d1.p1","form":"〜たびに","gloss":"every time …","connect":[{"pos":"Verb, dictionary form","rule":"会う＋{たびに}"},{"pos":"Noun for an event, such as 旅行 or 試験","rule":"〜の＋{たびに}"}],"examples":[{"ja":"[祖母|そぼ]に会う{たびに}、「大きくなったね」と言われます。","en":"Every time I see my grandmother, she tells me I have grown.","clip":"x_n3u01d1_p1_1"},{"ja":"試験の{たびに}、頭が[痛|いた]くなります。","en":"Every time there is an exam, I get a headache.","clip":"x_n3u01d1_p1_2"}],"watch":{"note":"たびに follows an event that happens again and again: a verb or a noun like 試験. It does not follow a length of time. For regular intervals, use ごとに.","bad":"三時間のたびに休みます。","good":"三時間ごとに休みます。"}},{"id":"n3u01d1.p2","form":"〜ごとに","gloss":"every (interval); each one","connect":[{"pos":"Noun: a length of time or a distance, with a number","rule":"〜＋{ごとに}（一時間ごとに・百メートルごとに）"},{"pos":"Noun: a thing or a person, each one in turn","rule":"〜＋{ごとに}（駅ごとに・人ごとに）"}],"examples":[{"ja":"この薬は八時間{ごとに}飲んでください。","en":"Please take this medicine every eight hours.","clip":"x_n3u01d1_p2_1"},{"ja":"クラス{ごとに}、テストの日が[違|ちが]います。","en":"The test date is different for each class.","clip":"x_n3u01d1_p2_2"}],"watch":{"note":"ごとに joins the noun directly. Unlike たびに, there is no の before it.","bad":"このバスは十分のごとに来ます。","good":"このバスは十分ごとに来ます。"}}],"compare":{"intro":"All three say that something happens again and again; たびに follows an event, while ごとに and おきに follow a noun, often a number.","forms":[{"form":"〜たびに","tag":"毎回 · every time","mark":"dot","ja":"この店に来る{たびに}、同じパンを買ってしまいます。","en":"Every time I come to this shop, I end up buying the same bread."},{"form":"〜ごとに","tag":"一つ一つ · every, each","mark":"dot","ja":"バスは十分{ごとに}来ます。","en":"The bus comes every ten minutes."},{"form":"〜おきに","tag":"一つ空けて · every other","mark":"dot","ja":"[一日|いちにち]{おきに}ジョギングをしています。","en":"I go jogging every other day. (With minutes and hours, 十分おきに and 十分ごとに mean the same.)"}],"check":{"id":"n3u01d1.c1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Which one takes の?","q":"父は^食事の^（　　）、この薬を飲んでいます。","options":["ごとに","たびに","おきに"],"answer":2,"why":["ごとに joins a noun directly, with no の: 食事ごとに.","An event as noun + の + たびに: every time he eats, he takes this medicine.","おきに also joins a noun directly, usually a number, as in 一日おきに."]}},"drill":[{"id":"n3u01d1.d1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"この写真を^見る^（　　）、国の家族を思い出します。","options":["までに","ように","たびに","あとで"],"answer":3,"why":["までに sets a deadline. Remembering your family is not something done by a deadline.","ように gives a goal or a way of doing something. Looking at a photo is neither here.","Dictionary form + たびに: each time I look at this photo, the same thing happens.","あとで follows the た form (見たあとで), not the dictionary form."]},{"id":"n3u01d1.d2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"引っ[越|こ]しをする（　　）、^いつも^物の多さにおどろきます。","options":["たびに","ために","までに","ように"],"answer":1,"why":["Every time I move house, I am surprised by how much stuff I have. いつも shows it happens each time.","ために with the dictionary form gives a purpose. Moving house is not done in order to be surprised.","までに sets a deadline, which does not fit a feeling.","ように gives a goal or a way of doing something. Being surprised is neither."]},{"id":"n3u01d1.d3","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"駅前から[空港|くうこう]まで、バスが^十五分^（　　）出ています。","options":["あいだに","たびに","のに","ごとに"],"answer":4,"why":["あいだに needs の after a noun (十五分のあいだに), and it means within one stretch of time, not over and over.","たびに follows an event. 十五分 is a length of time, not an event.","のに joins two clauses with a contrast. 十五分 is a noun, and there is no contrast here.","A length of time + ごとに: a bus leaves every fifteen minutes."]},{"id":"n3u01d1.d4","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"このホテルは、^[部屋|へや]^（　　）かべの色が[違|ちが]います。","options":["たびに","ごとに","までに","ばかりに"],"answer":2,"why":["たびに follows an event, as in とまるたびに. A room is not an event.","Noun + ごとに: each room has a different wall colour.","までに sets a deadline, and a room is not a time.","ばかりに gives a cause with a bad result, and it does not join a bare noun."]},{"id":"n3u01d1.d5","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"この歌を","after":"思い出します。","tiles":["聞く","たびに","楽しかった","ころを"],"star":2,"bank":[2,3,0,1],"hint":"この歌を needs a verb right after it. たびに follows the dictionary form.","full":"この歌を聞く{たびに}楽しかったころを思い出します。","explain":"この歌を goes with 聞く, and たびに follows the dictionary form. 楽しかった describes ころ, and ころを is what I remember: every time I hear this song, I remember happy times."},{"id":"n3u01d1.d6","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"このバスは","after":"時間がかかります。","tiles":["駅","ごとに","止まる","ので"],"star":2,"bank":[3,2,1,0],"hint":"ごとに joins a noun directly. ので follows a verb and gives the reason.","full":"このバスは駅{ごとに}止まるので時間がかかります。","explain":"駅ごとに (at every station) tells where the bus stops, so it comes before 止まる. ので follows 止まる and gives the reason it takes time."}],"exam":[{"id":"n3u01d1.e1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"人の前で話す（　　）、きんちょうして声が小さくなってしまう。","options":["たびに","までに","ために","ように"],"answer":1,"explain":"Every time I speak in front of people, I get nervous and my voice gets quiet: dictionary form + たびに, with the same result each time. までに sets a deadline, ために gives a purpose, and ように gives a goal or a way of doing something; none of them fits a result that happens each time."},{"id":"n3u01d1.e2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"この英語教室では、一か月（　　）席が変わります。","options":["たびに","ために","までに","ごとに"],"answer":4,"explain":"A length of time + ごとに: the seats change every month. たびに follows an event, not a length of time. ために gives a purpose or a cause, and までに sets a deadline; neither fits a change that repeats."},{"id":"n3u01d1.e3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"姉は","after":"おみやげを買ってきてくれる。","tiles":["旅行","の","たびに","おいしい"],"star":2,"bank":[3,2,0,1],"full":"姉は旅行の{たびに}おいしいおみやげを買ってきてくれる。","explain":"旅行, の, たびに, おいしい. A noun takes の before たびに, and おいしい must sit right before おみやげ: every time she travels, my sister brings back tasty souvenirs."}]},"scene":{"ja":"薬の飲み方","en":"How to take your medicine","intro":"The pharmacy gave you a sheet that says how to take your painkillers. Tap each word on it.","words":[{"id":"pharmacy","word":"薬局","reading":"やっきょく","gloss":"pharmacy","parts":[["薬","ヤッ","medicine"],["局","キョク","office, bureau"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d1_pharmacy"},{"id":"painkiller","word":"痛み止め","reading":"いたみどめ","gloss":"painkiller","parts":[["痛","いた","pain"],["止","ど","stop"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d1_painkiller"},{"id":"aftermeal","word":"食後","reading":"しょくご","gloss":"after meals","parts":[["食","ショク","eat, meal"],["後","ゴ","after"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d1_aftermeal"},{"id":"empty","word":"空腹時","reading":"くうふくじ","gloss":"on an empty stomach","parts":[["空","クウ","empty"],["腹","フク","stomach"],["時","ジ","time, when"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d1_empty"},{"id":"bedtime","word":"寝る前","reading":"ねるまえ","gloss":"before going to bed","parts":[["寝","ね","sleep, lie down"],["前","まえ","before"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d1_bedtime"},{"id":"always","word":"必ず","reading":"かならず","gloss":"always, without fail","parts":[["必","かなら","without fail"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d1_always"},{"id":"missed","word":"飲み忘れ","reading":"のみわすれ","gloss":"a missed dose","parts":[["飲","の","drink"],["忘","わす","forget"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d1_missed"},{"id":"drowsy","word":"眠気","reading":"ねむけ","gloss":"drowsiness","parts":[["眠","ねむ","sleep"],["気","け","feeling"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d1_drowsy"}],"check":{"id":"n3u01d1.k1","kind":"choice","type":"漢字読み","label":"How the exam asks it","q":"この薬を飲むと、_眠気_が出ることがあります。","options":["みんき","ねむけ","ねむき","みんけ"],"answer":2,"explain":"眠気 is read ねむけ, drowsiness: 眠 has its kun reading ねむ (as in 眠い), and 気 becomes け, as in 寒気. みんき and みんけ use the on reading ミン, and ねむき keeps き."}},"skill":{"kind":"listening","ja":"課題理解","en":"Task comprehension","ask":"男の人はこのあと、まず何をしますか。","audio":[["N","薬局で、女の人と男の人が話しています。男の人はこのあと、まず何をしますか。","やっきょくで、おんなのひととおとこのひとがはなしています。おとこのひとはこのあと、まずなにをしますか。"],["F","お待たせしました。こちらが痛み止めです。八時間ごとに一つ飲んでください。","おまたせしました。こちらがいたみどめです。はちじかんごとにひとつのんでください。"],["M","はい。食事のあとに飲むんですよね。","はい。しょくじのあとにのむんですよね。"],["F","ええ、できれば食後にお願いします。空腹時に飲むと、おなかが痛くなることがありますので。","ええ、できればしょくごにおねがいします。くうふくじにのむと、おなかがいたくなることがありますので。"],["M","実は、歯が痛くて、朝から何も食べていないんです。すぐに飲みたいんですが。","じつは、はがいたくて、あさからなにもたべていないんです。すぐにのみたいんですが。"],["F","でしたら、パンを少し食べてからでもだいじょうぶですよ。","でしたら、パンをすこしたべてからでもだいじょうぶですよ。"],["M","そうですか。あ、この薬を飲むと眠くなりますか。今日は車で来ているんです。","そうですか。あ、このくすりをのむとねむくなりますか。きょうはくるまできているんです。"],["F","飲むたびに眠くなる方もいます。飲んだあとは、運転しないでください。","のむたびにねむくなるかたもいます。のんだあとは、うんてんしないでください。"],["M","わかりました。じゃあ、家に帰ってから、何か食べて飲みます。","わかりました。じゃあ、いえにかえってから、なにかたべてのみます。"],["F","はい。お水はお持ちですか。","はい。おみずはおもちですか。"],["M","家にあるので、だいじょうぶです。","いえにあるので、だいじょうぶです。"],["N","男の人はこのあと、まず何をしますか。","おとこのひとはこのあと、まずなにをしますか。"]],"item":{"id":"n3u01d1.r1","kind":"choice","type":"課題理解","q":"男の人はこのあと、まず何をしますか。","script":["ナレーター：薬局で、女の人と男の人が話しています。男の人はこのあと、まず何をしますか。","女：お待たせしました。こちらが痛み止めです。八時間ごとに一つ飲んでください。","男：はい。食事のあとに飲むんですよね。","女：ええ、できれば食後にお願いします。空腹時に飲むと、おなかが痛くなることがありますので。","男：実は、歯が痛くて、朝から何も食べていないんです。すぐに飲みたいんですが。","女：でしたら、パンを少し食べてからでもだいじょうぶですよ。","男：そうですか。あ、この薬を飲むと眠くなりますか。今日は車で来ているんです。","女：飲むたびに眠くなる方もいます。飲んだあとは、運転しないでください。","男：わかりました。じゃあ、家に帰ってから、何か食べて飲みます。","女：はい。お水はお持ちですか。","男：家にあるので、だいじょうぶです。","ナレーター：男の人はこのあと、まず何をしますか。"],"options":["薬を飲む","パンを食べる","車で家に帰る","水を買う"],"printed":true,"short":["薬を飲む","パンを食べる","家に帰る","水を買う"],"answer":3,"why":["He wanted to take it at once, but he must not drive after taking it, so the medicine comes last.","The woman suggests bread, but he decides to go home first and eat there.","He came by car and must not drive after the medicine: 家に帰ってから、何か食べて飲みます. Going home comes first.","He has water at home (家にあるので), so he does not buy any."],"clip":"l_n3u1d1"}}},{"title":"〜おきに・〜ぶりに","grammar":{"points":[{"id":"n3u01d2.p1","form":"〜おきに","gloss":"at intervals of, every other …","connect":[{"pos":"Number + counter for time (日, 週間, か月, 年)","rule":"一日{おきに}、一週間{おきに}"},{"pos":"Number + counter for distance (here 〜ごとに means the same)","rule":"5メートル{おきに}"},{"pos":"Before a noun","rule":"一日{おきの}〜"}],"examples":[{"ja":"[祖父|そふ]は一日{おきに}病院に通っています。","en":"My grandfather goes to the hospital every other day.","clip":"x_n3u01d2_p1_1"},{"ja":"この道には、5メートル{おきに}花のプランターが[置|お]いてあります。","en":"There is a flower planter every five metres along this street.","clip":"x_n3u01d2_p1_2"}],"watch":{"note":"With time, おきに leaves a gap of one unit: 一日おきに is every other day, not every day. For every day, say 毎日.","bad":"このパン屋は休みがなく、一日おきに開いています。","good":"このパン屋は休みがなく、毎日開いています。"}},{"id":"n3u01d2.p2","form":"〜ぶりに・〜ぶりの","gloss":"for the first time in (a period)","connect":[{"pos":"Length of time (number + counter), before a verb","rule":"三年{ぶりに}会う"},{"pos":"Length of time, before a noun","rule":"十年{ぶりの}〜"},{"pos":"Length of time, at the end of a sentence","rule":"〜は五年{ぶりです}"}],"examples":[{"ja":"大学の友だちと、三年{ぶりに}会いました。","en":"I met a friend from university for the first time in three years.","clip":"x_n3u01d2_p2_1"},{"ja":"[昨日|きのう]、東京で十年{ぶりの}[大雪|おおゆき]が[降|ふ]りました。","en":"Yesterday Tokyo had its first heavy snow in ten years.","clip":"x_n3u01d2_p2_2"}],"watch":{"note":"ぶりに is about one event that happens again after a long gap. It does not mean \"for\" a length of time. For that, use 〜間.","bad":"日本に三年ぶりに住んでいます。","good":"日本に三年間住んでいます。"}}],"compare":{"intro":"With 一日 or 一年, おきに skips one (every other day) and ごとに does not (every day), while ぶりに marks one event after a long gap.","forms":[{"form":"〜おきに","tag":"一つとばして · every other","mark":"dot","ja":"[姉|あね]は一日{おきに}ジムに通っています。","en":"My sister goes to the gym every other day."},{"form":"〜ごとに","tag":"毎回 · every, each","mark":"dot","ja":"春になって、一日{ごとに}あたたかくなっています。","en":"Spring is here, and it gets warmer day by day."},{"form":"〜ぶりに","tag":"あいだがあいて · first time in","mark":"dot","ja":"夏休みに、三年{ぶりに}国へ帰りました。","en":"In the summer holidays, I went home for the first time in three years."}],"check":{"id":"n3u01d2.c1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Every day or every other day?","q":"父は毎日ではなく、一日（　　）ジョギングをしています。","options":["ごとに","ぶりに","おきに"],"answer":3,"why":["一日ごとに means every day, and 毎日ではなく rules that out.","ぶりに is for one event after a gap. Here jogging is a habit (しています).","Not every day but every other day: 一日おきに."]}},"drill":[{"id":"n3u01d2.d1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"駅前の道には、^五十メートル^（　　）ベンチが[置|お]いてあります。","options":["ぶりに","おきに","たびに","までに"],"answer":2,"why":["ぶりに needs a length of time and one event after a gap. 五十メートル is a distance.","Distance + おきに: there is a bench every fifty metres.","たびに follows a verb or a noun with の (行くたびに), not a distance.","までに gives a deadline. 五十メートルまでに does not make sense here."]},{"id":"n3u01d2.d2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"^先週^、五年（　　）テニスをしました。","options":["おきに","ごとに","間","ぶりに"],"answer":4,"why":["おきに is for something that repeats, but 先週 points to one game.","ごとに is also for something that repeats (every five years), not one game last week.","五年間テニスをしました says you played for five years, which does not fit 先週.","One game last week, after five years without tennis: 五年ぶりに."]},{"id":"n3u01d2.d3","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"この薬は強いので、一日（　　）、^二日に一回^だけ飲んでください。","options":["おきに","ごとに","ぶりに","までに"],"answer":1,"why":["一日おきに skips a day: once every two days, as 二日に一回 says.","一日ごとに means every day, which is not 二日に一回.","ぶりに is for one event after a gap, not a rule for taking medicine.","一日までに would be a deadline, which does not fit 二日に一回."]},{"id":"n3u01d2.d4","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"三年（　　）^ふるさと^は、ずいぶん[変|か]わっていました。","options":["ぶりに","おきの","ぶりの","ごとの"],"answer":3,"why":["ぶりに goes before a verb (三年ぶりに帰った). Here a noun, ふるさと, follows.","おきの is for things that come at intervals. The hometown does not.","Before a noun, ぶりの: my hometown, seen again after three years, had changed a lot.","ごとの is for things that repeat. The hometown does not."]},{"id":"n3u01d2.d5","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"医者に、","after":"言われました。","tiles":["一日","おきに","運動する","ように"],"star":2,"bank":[2,0,3,1],"hint":"おきに follows a number + counter. ように follows a verb in the dictionary form.","full":"医者に、一日{おきに}運動するように言われました。","explain":"一日おきに is one unit, and it tells when to exercise, so it comes before 運動する. ように follows the verb and comes right before 言われました: the doctor told me to exercise every other day."},{"id":"n3u01d2.d6","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"高校のクラス会で","after":"、少しも[変|か]わっていませんでした。","tiles":["十年","ぶりに","会った","友だちは"],"star":2,"bank":[3,1,0,2],"hint":"ぶりに follows a length of time and goes before a verb. Who had not changed?","full":"高校のクラス会で十年{ぶりに}会った友だちは、少しも[変|か]わっていませんでした。","explain":"十年ぶりに goes before the verb 会った, and 十年ぶりに会った describes 友だち. 友だちは is the topic of 変わっていませんでした, so it comes last."}],"exam":[{"id":"n3u01d2.e1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"この通りには、百メートル（　　）コンビニがあります。","options":["おきに","ぶりに","たびに","あとに"],"answer":1,"explain":"Distance + おきに: there is a convenience store every hundred metres. ぶりに needs a length of time and one event after a gap, たびに follows a verb or a noun with の, and あとに does not follow a distance."},{"id":"n3u01d2.e2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"大学を出てから一度も便りがなかった友人から、二十年（　　）手紙がとどきました。","options":["おきの","ごとの","までの","ぶりの"],"answer":4,"explain":"The friend sent nothing for twenty years, so this letter is one event after a long gap, and 手紙 is a noun: ぶりの. おきの and ごとの would mean letters came again and again, which 一度も rules out. 二十年までの手紙 does not make sense."},{"id":"n3u01d2.e3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"仕事が落ち着いたら、","after":"、海へ行くつもりです。","tiles":["二年","ぶりの","休みを","取って"],"star":2,"bank":[1,3,0,2],"full":"仕事が落ち着いたら、二年ぶりの{休みを}取って、海へ行くつもりです。","explain":"二年, ぶりの, 休みを, 取って. 二年ぶりの describes the noun 休み, 休みを is the object of 取って, and 取って joins the next part, 海へ行く: when work calms down, I will take my first holiday in two years and go to the sea."}]},"scene":{"ja":"同窓会のお知らせ","en":"A class reunion invitation","intro":"An invitation to a high school class reunion has come in the post. Tap each word on it.","words":[{"id":"reunion","word":"同窓会","reading":"どうそうかい","gloss":"class reunion","parts":[["同","ドウ","same"],["窓","ソウ","window: 窓口"],["会","カイ","meeting"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d2_reunion"},{"id":"invite","word":"招待","reading":"しょうたい","gloss":"invitation","parts":[["招","ショウ","invite"],["待","タイ","wait; treat"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d2_invite"},{"id":"join","word":"参加","reading":"さんか","gloss":"taking part","parts":[["参","サン","go, take part"],["加","カ","add"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d2_join"},{"id":"fee","word":"会費","reading":"かいひ","gloss":"fee for the event","parts":[["会","カイ","meeting"],["費","ヒ","cost: 交通費"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d2_fee"},{"id":"rsvp","word":"出欠","reading":"しゅっけつ","gloss":"attending or not","parts":[["出","シュッ","attend, go out"],["欠","ケツ","lack, be absent"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d2_rsvp"},{"id":"reply","word":"返信","reading":"へんしん","gloss":"reply (by post or email)","parts":[["返","ヘン","return"],["信","シン","message; trust"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d2_reply"},{"id":"desk","word":"受付","reading":"うけつけ","gloss":"reception desk","parts":[["受","う","receive"],["付","つけ","attach"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d2_desk"},{"id":"photo","word":"記念写真","reading":"きねんしゃしん","gloss":"group photo to remember the day","parts":[["記","キ","record"],["念","ネン","thought"],["写","シャ","copy"],["真","シン","true"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d2_photo"}],"check":{"id":"n3u01d2.k1","kind":"choice","type":"漢字読み","label":"How the exam asks it","q":"同窓会の_出欠_は、はがきで知らせてください。","options":["しゅつけつ","しゅっきつ","しゅっけつ","でけつ"],"answer":3,"explain":"出欠 is read しゅっけつ: 出 becomes しゅっ before け, and 欠 is けつ. しゅつけつ has no small っ, しゅっきつ has き instead of け, and でけつ uses the wrong reading of 出."}},"skill":{"kind":"reading","ja":"内容理解（短文）","en":"Short passage","ask":"What does the reader of this message have to do?","seconds":90,"passage":"三年二組のみなさん、お元気ですか。山田です。高校を出てから、今年でちょうど十年になります。そこで、十年ぶりにクラスの同窓会を開くことにしました。日時は十一月二十三日（日）午後六時から、場所は駅前のレストラン「さくら」です。会費は五千円で、^当日、受付で^お願いします。田中先生も来てくださる予定です。^出欠は、十月三十一日までに、このメールに返信して知らせてください^。来られない人も、今どうしているか、ひとこと書いてくれるとうれしいです。これからは一年おきに^集まれたらいいなと思っています^。","strategy":"Skip the dates of the party itself and look for a request: 〜てください and the date that goes with it.","item":{"id":"n3u01d2.r1","kind":"choice","type":"読解・内容理解（短文）","q":"このメールを読んだ人がしなければならないことは何か。","options":["十月三十一日までに、会費を払う。","来られるかどうかを、十月三十一日までにメールで知らせる。","一年おきに集まれるかどうか、返事をする。","来られない場合は、田中先生にそのことを伝える。"],"short":["会費を払う","出欠をメールで知らせる","一年おきに集まれるか返事する","田中先生に伝える"],"answer":2,"explain":"The request is 出欠は、十月三十一日までに、このメールに返信して知らせてください: everyone replies by email, by 31 October, to say whether they can come.","why":["The fee is paid on the day, at the reception desk (当日、受付で).","","Meeting every other year is only Yamada's hope (集まれたらいいな). Nobody is asked to answer it.","Teacher Tanaka is coming, but people who cannot come reply to this email, not to him."]}}},{"title":"〜て以来・〜てはじめて","grammar":{"points":[{"id":"n3u01d3.p1","form":"〜て以来","gloss":"ever since …","connect":[{"pos":"Verb, te-form","rule":"日本に来て{以来}"},{"pos":"Noun for a past event, such as 入社 or 開店 (a little formal)","rule":"〜{以来}"},{"pos":"On its own, after an event just mentioned","rule":"それ{以来}"}],"examples":[{"ja":"この町に引っ[越|こ]して{以来}、毎朝川の近くを歩いています。","en":"Ever since I moved to this town, I have walked by the river every morning.","clip":"x_n3u01d3_p1_1"},{"ja":"父は去年たばこをやめて{以来}、一度も[吸|す]っていません。","en":"My father has not smoked once since he quit last year.","clip":"x_n3u01d3_p1_2"}],"watch":{"note":"以来 needs a state or habit that has gone on from then until now. For one event that happened afterwards, use てから.","bad":"日本に来て以来、すぐ友だちができました。","good":"日本に来てから、すぐ友だちができました。"}},{"id":"n3u01d3.p2","form":"〜てはじめて","gloss":"only after … (did one realise)","connect":[{"pos":"Verb, te-form","rule":"親になって{はじめて}"},{"pos":"What follows: a new understanding, or something only now possible","rule":"〜て{はじめて}、分かる／気づく／できるようになる"}],"examples":[{"ja":"海外に住んで{はじめて}、自分の国のことをよく知らないと気づきました。","en":"Only after living abroad did I notice how little I knew about my own country.","clip":"x_n3u01d3_p2_1"},{"ja":"[実際|じっさい]に使って{はじめて}、この[道具|どうぐ]の[便利|べんり]さが分かりました。","en":"Only after actually using this tool did I see how handy it is.","clip":"x_n3u01d3_p2_2"}],"watch":{"note":"The second half is something you only now understand or can do. It cannot be a request, an invitation or a plan.","bad":"日本に来てはじめて、すしを食べに行きましょう。","good":"日本に来てはじめて、本当のすしの味を知りました。"}}],"compare":{"intro":"All three follow a te-form and look back at an earlier event. What changes is what comes after it.","forms":[{"form":"〜て以来","tag":"それからずっと · ever since","mark":"dot","ja":"[祖父|そふ]は[退職|たいしょく]して{以来}、毎朝[庭|にわ]の花の世話をしています。","en":"Ever since he retired, my grandfather has looked after the flowers in the garden every morning."},{"form":"〜てはじめて","tag":"やっと気づく · only after","mark":"dot","ja":"自分で店を持って{はじめて}、[商売|しょうばい]の[難|むずか]しさが分かりました。","en":"Only after having my own shop did I understand how hard business is."},{"form":"〜てから","tag":"順番 · after, then","mark":"dot","ja":"毎朝パンを作って{から}、店を開けます。","en":"Every morning I make the bread, then open the shop."}],"check":{"id":"n3u01d3.c1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"仕事のあとで","q":"店を[閉|し]めて（　　）、みんなで食事に行きましょう。","options":["以来","はじめて","から"],"answer":3,"why":["以来 needs a state or habit that has gone on since then, and it cannot lead to an invitation like 行きましょう.","はじめて needs a new understanding or ability after it, not an invitation.","One action after another: close the shop, then go and eat. てから fits plans and invitations."]}},"drill":[{"id":"n3u01d3.d1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"[彼|かれ]は二年前に[転職|てんしょく]（　　）、^ずっと^毎日楽しそうに働いています。","options":["するたびに","して以来","するために","してはじめて"],"answer":2,"why":["たびに is for every time something happens. 二年前に points to one event, not a repeated one.","One past event, and a state that has gone on since then: ずっと…働いています.","ために gives a purpose. Changing jobs is not the purpose of working happily.","はじめて needs a new understanding or ability after it. ずっと…ています describes a lasting state instead."]},{"id":"n3u01d3.d2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"^仕事を[失|うしな]って^（　　）、毎日働けることのありがたさが分かりました。","options":["以来","もらって","はじめて","おいて"],"answer":3,"why":["以来 needs a state or habit that has gone on since then. 分かりました here is one moment of understanding.","てもらう means someone does something for you. Nobody lost a job for the speaker.","Only after losing the job did the speaker understand: てはじめて + 分かりました.","ておく is for doing something in advance on purpose. Nobody loses a job to get ready for something."]},{"id":"n3u01d3.d3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"[祖母|そぼ]は","after":"あまり出なくなりました。","tiles":["足を","[痛|いた]めて","以来","外に"],"star":1,"bank":[3,2,0,1],"hint":"以来 follows the te-form. What did she hurt, and where does she not go any more?","full":"[祖母|そぼ]は足を[痛|いた]めて{以来}外にあまり出なくなりました。","explain":"足を goes with 痛めて, and 以来 follows the te-form. 外に goes with 出なくなりました: since she hurt her leg, she has hardly gone out."},{"id":"n3u01d3.d4","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"会社に着いて（　　）、^すぐに^[部長|ぶちょう]に[呼|よ]ばれました。","options":["から","以来","はじめて","ばかりで"],"answer":1,"why":["One event right after another: てから. すぐに shows it happened straight after arriving.","以来 needs something that has gone on until now. Being called once is a single event.","はじめて needs a new understanding or ability after it. Being called by the manager is neither.","てばかり means doing only one thing again and again, which does not fit 着く. \"Had just arrived\" would be 着いたばかりで."]},{"id":"n3u01d3.d5","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"^自分で家事をして^（　　）、母の[苦労|くろう]が分かりました。","options":["も","以来","もらって","はじめて"],"answer":4,"why":["ても means even if or even though. Doing the housework is the reason the speaker understands, not something against it.","以来 needs a state or habit that has gone on since then. 分かりました is one moment of understanding.","てもらう means someone else does it for you, but 自分で says the speaker did it.","Only after doing the housework herself did the speaker understand: てはじめて + 分かりました."]},{"id":"n3u01d3.d6","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"[実際|じっさい]に店で","after":"分かるようになりました。","tiles":["働いて","はじめて","お[客|きゃく]さんの","気持ちが"],"star":2,"bank":[2,0,3,1],"hint":"はじめて follows the te-form. Whose feelings did the speaker come to understand?","full":"[実際|じっさい]に店で働いて{はじめて}お[客|きゃく]さんの気持ちが分かるようになりました。","explain":"店で goes with 働いて, and はじめて follows the te-form. お客さんの describes 気持ちが, which goes with 分かるようになりました."}],"exam":[{"id":"n3u01d3.e1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"この店は十年前に（　　）、ずっと同じ味を守っています。","options":["開店するたびに","開店して以来","開店してはじめて","開店したばかりで"],"answer":2,"explain":"One past event (十年前に) and a state that has gone on since then (ずっと…守っています): して以来. たびに needs a repeated event, はじめて needs a new understanding after it, and ばかり (just opened) does not fit ten years ago."},{"id":"n3u01d3.e2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"社会に出て（　　）、学生時代がどんなに楽だったかが分かった。","options":["はじめて","以来","おいて","ばかりで"],"answer":1,"explain":"Only after starting work did the speaker realise how easy student life was: てはじめて + 分かった. 以来 needs a state that has gone on, not one moment of understanding. ておく is for preparing in advance, and 出てばかりで does not make sense here."},{"id":"n3u01d3.e3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"二人は","after":"親しくしています。","tiles":["二十年前に","知り合って","以来","ずっと"],"star":1,"bank":[3,0,2,1],"full":"二人は二十年前に{知り合って}以来ずっと親しくしています。","explain":"二十年前に, 知り合って, 以来, ずっと. 二十年前に goes with 知り合って, 以来 follows the te-form, and ずっと goes with the lasting state 親しくしています."}]},"scene":{"ja":"開店三十年記念のお知らせ","en":"A shop's thirtieth-anniversary notice","intro":"A notice in a bakery window marks thirty years since the shop opened. Tap each word on it.","words":[{"id":"memorial","word":"記念","reading":"きねん","gloss":"commemoration, to mark (an event)","parts":[["記","キ","record"],["念","ネン","thought"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d3_memorial"},{"id":"ourshop","word":"当店","reading":"とうてん","gloss":"this shop, our shop","parts":[["当","トウ","this, the one in question"],["店","テン","shop"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d3_ourshop"},{"id":"everyone","word":"皆様","reading":"みなさま","gloss":"everyone (polite)","parts":[["皆","みな","everyone"],["様","さま","polite title"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d3_everyone"},{"id":"support","word":"支える","reading":"ささえる","gloss":"to support","parts":[["支","ささ","support"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d3_support"},{"id":"period","word":"期間","reading":"きかん","gloss":"period (of time)","parts":[["期","キ","period"],["間","カン","interval"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d3_period"},{"id":"limited","word":"限定","reading":"げんてい","gloss":"limited, only","parts":[["限","ゲン","limit"],["定","テイ","fixed"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d3_limited"},{"id":"goods","word":"商品","reading":"しょうひん","gloss":"goods, products","parts":[["商","ショウ","trade"],["品","ヒン","goods"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d3_goods"},{"id":"discount","word":"割引","reading":"わりびき","gloss":"discount","parts":[["割","わり","divide"],["引","びき","pull"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d3_discount"}],"check":{"id":"n3u01d3.k1","kind":"choice","type":"漢字読み","label":"How the exam asks it","q":"このパンは週末_限定_です。","options":["けんてい","げんじょう","かんてい","げんてい"],"answer":4,"explain":"限定 is read げんてい: this bread is sold only at the weekend. けんてい has け instead of げ, げんじょう is a different word (現状, the present state), and かんてい reads 限 as かん."}},"skill":{"kind":"listening","ja":"ポイント理解","en":"Point comprehension","ask":"男の人は、どうしてパン屋を始めましたか。","audio":[["N","パン屋で、女の人と店の男の人が話しています。男の人は、どうしてパン屋を始めましたか。","パンやで、おんなのひととみせのおとこのひとがはなしています。おとこのひとは、どうしてパンやをはじめましたか。"],["F","開店三十年、おめでとうございます。","かいてんさんじゅうねん、おめでとうございます。"],["M","ありがとうございます。店を開いて以来、毎朝四時に起きてパンを作っています。","ありがとうございます。みせをひらいていらい、まいあさよじにおきてパンをつくっています。"],["F","子どものころから、パン屋さんになりたかったんですか。",null],["M","いいえ。前は会社員で、パンにはあまりきょうみがなかったんです。","いいえ。まえはかいしゃいんで、パンにはあまりきょうみがなかったんです。"],["F","え、そうなんですか。じゃあ、会社のお仕事が大変だったとか…。",null],["M","いえ、仕事は忙しかったですが、楽しかったですよ。ただ、仕事でフランスに行ったとき、小さな店でパンを食べたんです。それを食べてはじめて、本当においしいパンがどんなものか分かりました。それで、自分でも作りたくなったんです。",null],["F","ご家族は賛成してくださいましたか。",null],["M","いえ、妻には反対されましたよ。でも、今はいっしょに店をやっています。","いえ、つまにははんたいされましたよ。でも、いまはいっしょにみせをやっています。"],["N","男の人は、どうしてパン屋を始めましたか。","おとこのひとは、どうしてパンやをはじめましたか。"]],"item":{"id":"n3u01d3.r1","kind":"choice","type":"ポイント理解","q":"男の人は、どうしてパン屋を始めましたか。","script":["ナレーター：パン屋で、女の人と店の男の人が話しています。男の人は、どうしてパン屋を始めましたか。","女：開店三十年、おめでとうございます。","男：ありがとうございます。店を開いて以来、毎朝四時に起きてパンを作っています。","女：子どものころから、パン屋さんになりたかったんですか。","男：いいえ。前は会社員で、パンにはあまりきょうみがなかったんです。","女：え、そうなんですか。じゃあ、会社のお仕事が大変だったとか…。","男：いえ、仕事は忙しかったですが、楽しかったですよ。ただ、仕事でフランスに行ったとき、小さな店でパンを食べたんです。それを食べてはじめて、本当においしいパンがどんなものか分かりました。それで、自分でも作りたくなったんです。","女：ご家族は賛成してくださいましたか。","男：いえ、妻には反対されましたよ。でも、今はいっしょに店をやっています。","ナレーター：男の人は、どうしてパン屋を始めましたか。"],"options":["会社の仕事が大変だったから","フランスで食べたパンがおいしかったから","家族にすすめられたから","子どものころからパン屋になりたかったから"],"printed":true,"short":["仕事が大変","フランスのパン","家族のすすめ","子どものころの夢"],"answer":2,"why":["He says his job was busy but fun: 忙しかったですが、楽しかったですよ.","Only after eating that bread in France did he understand what really good bread is (食べてはじめて…分かりました), and then he wanted to make it himself.","His family did not suggest it. His wife was against it at first: 妻には反対されました.","He says no: he was an office worker and not very interested in bread."],"clip":"l_n3u1d3"}}},{"title":"〜ところに・〜ところを","grammar":{"points":[{"id":"n3u01d4.p1","form":"〜ところに／〜ところへ","gloss":"just when … (someone came, something happened)","connect":[{"pos":"Verb, ている form","rule":"〜ている ＋ {ところに}／{ところへ}"},{"pos":"Verb, volitional form + とする","rule":"〜ようとしている／〜ようとした ＋ {ところに}"},{"pos":"Verb, た form","rule":"〜た ＋ {ところに}"}],"examples":[{"ja":"会社を出ようとした{ところに}、[部長|ぶちょう]から電話がかかってきました。","en":"Just as I was about to leave the office, my manager phoned.","clip":"x_n3u01d4_p1_1"},{"ja":"みんなで昼ご飯を食べている{ところへ}、社長が入ってきました。","en":"Just as we were all eating lunch, the company president walked in.","clip":"x_n3u01d4_p1_2"}],"watch":{"note":"What comes after ところに is something that happens to you or someone who arrives, often an interruption. For something you do yourself at the same time, use ながら or 〜ているとき.","bad":"料理をしているところに、わたしはラジオを聞きました。","good":"料理をしながら、ラジオを聞きました。"}},{"id":"n3u01d4.p2","form":"〜ところを","gloss":"(seen or caught) in the middle of","connect":[{"pos":"Verb, ている form or た form","rule":"〜ている／〜た ＋ {ところを}"},{"pos":"い-adjective, in set phrases of thanks","rule":"お[忙|いそが]しい ＋ {ところを}"},{"pos":"Noun + の, in set phrases of thanks","rule":"お休みの ＋ {ところを}"}],"examples":[{"ja":"[会議中|かいぎちゅう]に[寝|ね]ている{ところを}、[部長|ぶちょう]に見られてしまいました。","en":"My manager saw me sleeping in the meeting.","clip":"x_n3u01d4_p2_1"},{"ja":"お[忙|いそが]しい{ところを}[手伝|てつだ]っていただいて、ありがとうございました。","en":"Thank you for helping me when you were so busy.","clip":"x_n3u01d4_p2_2"}],"watch":{"note":"ところを is the scene someone sees or catches, so it takes を before verbs like 見る, 見られる and 見つかる. ところに would need someone arriving, as in 母が来た.","bad":"たばこをすっているところに、母に見られました。","good":"たばこをすっているところを、母に見られました。"}}],"compare":{"intro":"All three use ところ for one moment in an action, and what follows ところ decides the meaning.","forms":[{"form":"〜ところに","tag":"ちょうどそのとき · just then, something came","mark":"dot","ja":"[寝|ね]ようとした{ところに}、電話が[鳴|な]りました。","en":"Just as I was going to bed, the phone rang."},{"form":"〜ところを","tag":"見られる · seen in the middle of","mark":"dot","ja":"一人で歌っている{ところを}、妹に見られました。","en":"My sister saw me singing on my own."},{"form":"〜ところだ（N4）","tag":"動作の時 · about to, doing, just did","mark":"dot","ja":"今から出かける{ところです}。","en":"I'm just about to go out."}],"check":{"id":"n3u01d4.c1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Which ところ?","q":"ゲームで[遊|あそ]んでいる（　　）、父に見られてしまいました。","options":["ところに","ところを","ところです"],"answer":2,"why":["ところに is followed by something that arrives or happens. 見られる needs the scene as its object, so を.","Father saw the scene: ところを ＋ 見られる.","ところです ends a sentence. It cannot join the next clause with a comma."]}},"drill":[{"id":"n3u01d4.d1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"[部屋|へや]をそうじしている（　　）、^友だちが急に[遊|あそ]びに来ました^。","options":["ところを","たびに","ところに","ところだ"],"answer":3,"why":["ところを needs a verb like 見る or 見つかる after it. 友だちが来る does not take it as an object.","たびに means every time and follows the dictionary form. Here it is one visit that came out of the blue (急に).","In the middle of cleaning, a friend arrived: ている ＋ ところに.","ところだ ends a sentence, so it cannot join the next clause."]},{"id":"n3u01d4.d2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"電車の中で[寝|ね]ている（　　）、友だちに^写真をとられて^しまいました。","options":["ところに","ところを","たびに","[以来|いらい]"],"answer":2,"why":["写真をとられる needs the scene as its object. ところに would need someone arriving, as in 友だちが来た.","The friend photographed the scene of me sleeping: ところを ＋ とられる.","たびに follows the dictionary form and means every time. This is one event.","以来 follows the て form (寝て以来) and means ever since. It does not fit here."]},{"id":"n3u01d4.d3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"ちょうどシャワーを","after":"人が来ました。","tiles":["あびて","いる","ところへ","[宅配便|たくはいびん]の"],"star":3,"bank":[2,3,0,1],"hint":"シャワーを takes a verb. Which tile describes 人?","full":"ちょうどシャワーをあびているところへ[宅配便|たくはいびん]の人が来ました。","explain":"シャワーをあびている is what I was doing. ところへ comes after it, and the person who arrived follows: 宅配便の人が来ました."},{"id":"n3u01d4.d4","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"お[忙|いそが]しい（　　）、^[資料|しりょう]を見ていただいて^ありがとうございました。","options":["たびに","うちに","ところだ","ところを"],"answer":4,"why":["たびに means every time, and it does not follow お忙しい. This is a thank-you for one favour.","うちに means before a change comes. Here the speaker thanks someone; nothing is about to change.","ところだ ends a sentence, so it cannot join the thanks that follows.","The set phrase of thanks: お忙しいところを ＋ 〜ていただいて, ありがとうございました."]},{"id":"n3u01d4.d5","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"すみません、今から^[会議|かいぎ]が始まる^（　　）。あとでこちらから電話します。","options":["ところなんです","ところに","ところを","たびに"],"answer":1,"why":["Dictionary form ＋ ところだ: the meeting is about to start. なんです explains why the speaker cannot talk now.","ところに needs a clause after it in the same sentence. Here the sentence ends.","ところを also needs a verb after it, such as 見られる. Here the sentence ends.","たびに means every time, and it also needs a clause after it."]},{"id":"n3u01d4.d6","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"お休みの","after":"、ありがとうございました。","tiles":["ところを","わざわざ","来て","いただき"],"star":1,"bank":[3,1,0,2],"hint":"お休みの needs a noun right after it. Where does わざわざ (taking the trouble) go?","full":"お休みのところをわざわざ来ていただき、ありがとうございました。","explain":"お休みのところを is the set phrase. わざわざ comes before the verb it describes, and 来ていただき joins the thanks."}],"exam":[{"id":"n3u01d4.e1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"夕飯を作っている（　　）、となりの人が野菜を持ってきてくれた。","options":["ところに","ところを","たびに","ところだ"],"answer":1,"explain":"In the middle of cooking, the neighbour arrived with vegetables: ている ＋ ところに. ところを needs a verb like 見る after it, たびに follows the dictionary form and means every time, and ところだ ends a sentence."},{"id":"n3u01d4.e2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"弟はれいぞうこのケーキをこっそり食べている（　　）、母に見つかってしまった。","options":["ところに","ごとに","ところを","以来"],"answer":3,"explain":"見つかる takes the scene as its object: 食べているところを見つかった. ところに would need someone arriving, as in 母が来た. ごとに follows a noun or the dictionary form, and 以来 follows the て form."},{"id":"n3u01d4.e3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"アルバイト中にゲームを","after":"見つかってしまった。","tiles":["して","いる","ところを","店長に"],"star":2,"bank":[3,2,0,1],"full":"アルバイト中にゲームをしている{ところを}店長に見つかってしまった。","explain":"して, いる, ところを, 店長に. ゲームをしている is the scene, ところを makes it the thing found, and 店長に shows who found it."}]},"scene":{"ja":"伝言メモ","en":"An office message pad","intro":"Tap every word you would have to read on the message slip.","words":[{"id":"message","word":"伝言","reading":"でんごん","gloss":"message (left for someone)","parts":[["伝","デン","pass on"],["言","ゴン","words"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d4_message"},{"id":"honorific","word":"様","reading":"さま","gloss":"Mr, Ms (polite, after a name)","parts":[["様","さま","polite title: お客様"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d4_honorific"},{"id":"absent","word":"不在","reading":"ふざい","gloss":"away, not in","parts":[["不","フ","not"],["在","ザイ","be present"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d4_absent"},{"id":"matter","word":"用件","reading":"ようけん","gloss":"what the call is about","parts":[["用","ヨウ","business"],["件","ケン","matter: 事件"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d4_matter"},{"id":"callback","word":"折り返し","reading":"おりかえし","gloss":"calling back","parts":[["折","お","fold"],["返","かえ","return"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d4_callback"},{"id":"back","word":"戻り","reading":"もどり","gloss":"return (time back at the desk)","parts":[["戻","もど","come back"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d4_back"},{"id":"reply","word":"返事","reading":"へんじ","gloss":"reply, answer","parts":[["返","ヘン","return"],["事","ジ","thing"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d4_reply"},{"id":"confirm","word":"確認","reading":"かくにん","gloss":"check, confirmation","parts":[["確","カク","certain"],["認","ニン","recognise"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d4_confirm"}],"check":{"id":"n3u01d4.k1","kind":"choice","type":"漢字読み","label":"How the exam asks it","q":"_不在_の間に、お客様から電話がありました。","options":["ぶざい","ふさい","ふざい","ふうざい"],"answer":3,"explain":"不在 is read ふざい: while you were out, a customer phoned. ぶざい uses the ぶ of 不用心, which is not this word, ふさい has さ instead of ざ, and ふうざい adds a long う."}},"skill":{"kind":"reading","ja":"内容理解（中文）","en":"Mid-length passage","ask":"Who did what, and what happened as a result?","seconds":100,"passage":"山田さん、先日はお忙しいところを引っ越しの手伝いに来ていただき、本当にありがとうございました。あの日の朝は、にもつが多くて、一人ではとても終わらないと思っていました。困っているところに山田さんが車で来てくださって、本当に助かりました。おかげで、^夕方には全部運び終わりました^。ただ、^わたしが大切なおさらを割ってしまったところを山田さんに見られて^、少し恥ずかしかったです。来月、部屋がかたづいたら、^ぜひ食事に来てください^。料理を作ってお待ちしています。","strategy":"Check who did each thing: who broke the plate, who saw it, and who is invited where.","item":{"id":"n3u01d4.r1","kind":"choice","type":"読解・内容理解（中文）","q":"この手紙の内容に合うものはどれか。","options":["引っ越しの日、山田さんが来る前ににもつを全部運んでいた。","山田さんがおさらを割ったところを見て、恥ずかしく思った。","山田さんに手伝ってもらったので、その日の夕方には運び終わった。","来月、山田さんの家へ食事に行くことになっている。"],"short":["山田さんが来る前に運んでいた","山田さんが割ったのを見た","手伝ってもらい夕方に運び終わった","山田さんの家へ食事に行く"],"answer":3,"explain":"困っているところに山田さんが来てくださって and おかげで、夕方には全部運び終わりました: with Yamada's help the moving was done by evening.","why":["The writer thought she could not finish alone, and was still struggling when Yamada arrived (困っているところに).","It is the other way round. The writer broke the plate, and Yamada saw it (ところを山田さんに見られて).","","The writer invites Yamada to her own new place (食事に来てください), not the other way round."]}}},{"title":"〜最中に・〜たとたん（に）","grammar":{"points":[{"id":"n3u01d5.p1","form":"〜最中に","gloss":"right in the middle of","connect":[{"pos":"Noun","rule":"〜の＋{[最中|さいちゅう]に}"},{"pos":"Verb, ている form","rule":"〜ている＋{[最中|さいちゅう]に}"},{"pos":"At the end of a sentence","rule":"〜の／〜ている＋{[最中|さいちゅう]です}"}],"examples":[{"ja":"[会議|かいぎ]の{[最中|さいちゅう]に}、急に電気が[消|き]えました。","en":"Right in the middle of the meeting, the lights suddenly went out.","clip":"x_n3u01d5_p1_1"},{"ja":"友だちと電話で話している{[最中|さいちゅう]に}、スマホの電池が切れてしまいました。","en":"Right in the middle of a phone call with a friend, my phone battery died.","clip":"x_n3u01d5_p1_2"}],"watch":{"note":"With a verb, use the ている form: 最中 means the action is still going on. The dictionary form does not join 最中. What follows is usually something that breaks in.","bad":"会議をする最中に、電話が鳴りました。","good":"会議をしている最中に、電話が鳴りました。"}},{"id":"n3u01d5.p2","form":"〜たとたん（に）","gloss":"the moment … (something unexpected)","connect":[{"pos":"Verb, た form","rule":"開けた＋{とたん}"},{"pos":"Verb, た form, with に","rule":"着いた＋{とたんに}"}],"examples":[{"ja":"エアコンをつけた{とたんに}、[部屋|へや]の電気が[消|き]えました。","en":"The moment I turned on the air conditioner, the lights in the room went out.","clip":"x_n3u01d5_p2_1"},{"ja":"家に着いた{とたん}、雨が[降|ふ]ってきました。","en":"The moment I got home, it started to rain.","clip":"x_n3u01d5_p2_2"}],"watch":{"note":"とたん tells what happened at once, often a surprise. After it, do not put your own plan, a request or an invitation. For those, use 〜たらすぐ.","bad":"駅に着いたとたん、電話してください。","good":"駅に着いたらすぐ、電話してください。"}}],"compare":{"intro":"All three tell when something happens: in the middle of an action, the instant after it, or simply right after it.","forms":[{"form":"〜最中に","tag":"している間 · right in the middle","mark":"dot","ja":"試合の{[最中|さいちゅう]に}、雨が[降|ふ]ってきました。","en":"Right in the middle of the match, it started to rain."},{"form":"〜たとたん","tag":"その時すぐ · the instant (a surprise)","mark":"dot","ja":"試合が始まった{とたん}、雨が[降|ふ]ってきました。","en":"The instant the match started, it began to rain."},{"form":"〜たらすぐ","tag":"あとすぐ · as soon as (plans are fine)","mark":"dot","ja":"試合が終わっ{たらすぐ}、家に帰りましょう。","en":"As soon as the match is over, let's go home."}],"check":{"id":"n3u01d5.c1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Which one takes an invitation?","q":"仕事が（　　）、飲みに行きましょう。","options":["終わる[最中|さいちゅう]に","終わったとたん","終わったらすぐ"],"answer":3,"why":["[最中|さいちゅう] joins a noun with の or the ている form. Also, 終わる is over in a moment, so it has no middle.","行きましょう is an invitation, and an invitation cannot follow とたん.","たらすぐ can take an invitation: as soon as work is over, let's go for a drink."]}},"drill":[{"id":"n3u01d5.d1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"大事な電話をしている（　　）、^となりの[部屋|へや]から大きな音がしました^。","options":["とたんに","[最中|さいちゅう]に","あとで","ところを"],"answer":2,"why":["とたんに follows the た form, as in 電話をしたとたんに. Here the verb is している.","ている + [最中|さいちゅう]に: right in the middle of the call, a loud noise broke in.","あとで follows the た form or a noun with の, not the ている form.","ところを needs a verb after it that acts on the person in that scene, such as 見られる or じゃまする. 音がしました is not one."]},{"id":"n3u01d5.d2","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"わたしが","after":"、家中の電気が[消|き]えました。","tiles":["ドライヤーの","スイッチを","入れた","とたん"],"star":2,"bank":[2,3,1,0],"hint":"とたん follows the た form. What did the speaker turn on, and the switch of what?","full":"わたしがドライヤーのスイッチを入れた{とたん}、家中の電気が[消|き]えました。","explain":"ドライヤーの describes スイッチ, and スイッチを is what 入れた takes. とたん comes right after the た form 入れた: the moment I switched on the hair dryer, every light in the house went out."},{"id":"n3u01d5.d3","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose what follows","q":"げんかんのドアを開けた^とたん^、（　　）。","options":["中に入ってください","中に入りましょう","ねこが外に[飛|と]び出しました","中に入ろうと思います"],"answer":3,"why":["This is a request, and a request cannot follow とたん.","This is an invitation, and an invitation cannot follow とたん.","Something the speaker did not plan happened at once: the cat shot out of the door.","This is the speaker's own plan (〜ようと思います), which cannot follow とたん."]},{"id":"n3u01d5.d4","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"すみません、^今は食事の^（　　）なので、あとでこちらから電話します。","options":["[最中|さいちゅう]","とたん","たび","ごと"],"answer":1,"why":["Noun + の + [最中|さいちゅう] at the end of a clause: I am in the middle of a meal right now.","とたん follows the た form of a verb, not a noun with の.","たび means every time. It takes に and a repeated event after it; it does not say what is going on now.","ごと joins a noun directly, without の (一日ごと), and means every."]},{"id":"n3u01d5.d5","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"子どもは^母親の[顔|かお]を見た^（　　）、なき出しました。","options":["[最中|さいちゅう]に","うちに","まえに","とたん"],"answer":4,"why":["[最中|さいちゅう] needs a noun with の or the ている form. 見た is the た form.","うちに follows the ている form or the dictionary form, not the た form.","まえに follows the dictionary form: 見るまえに.","た form + とたん: the moment the child saw his mother's face, he burst into tears."]},{"id":"n3u01d5.d6","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"社長が","after":"、だれかのスマホが[鳴|な]りました。","tiles":["新しい","計画を","説明している","[最中|さいちゅう]に"],"star":1,"bank":[2,0,3,1],"hint":"[最中|さいちゅう] follows the ている form. What is the president explaining?","full":"社長が新しい計画を説明している{[最中|さいちゅう]に}、だれかのスマホが[鳴|な]りました。","explain":"新しい describes 計画, and 計画を is what 説明している takes. [最中|さいちゅう]に comes right after the ている form: right in the middle of the president's talk, someone's phone rang."}],"exam":[{"id":"n3u01d5.e1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"サッカーの試合の（　　）、急に強い雨が降ってきました。","options":["とたんに","うえに","最中に","ところに"],"answer":3,"explain":"Noun + の + 最中に: right in the middle of the match, heavy rain started. とたんに follows the た form of a verb, not a noun with の. 試合のうえに and 試合のところに would mean on top of the match and at the match's place, which make no sense here."},{"id":"n3u01d5.e2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"家に着いた（　　）、雨が強く降ってきました。","options":["最中に","うちに","までに","とたん"],"answer":4,"explain":"着いた is the た form, and the rain started at that very moment: とたん. 最中に needs a noun with の or the ている form. うちに and までに do not follow the た form."},{"id":"n3u01d5.e3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"ドライヤーで","after":"消えてしまいました。","tiles":["かみを","かわかしている","最中に","家の電気が"],"star":1,"bank":[3,1,0,2],"full":"ドライヤーでかみを{かわかしている}最中に家の電気が消えてしまいました。","explain":"かみを, かわかしている, 最中に, 家の電気が. かみを goes with かわかしている, 最中に follows the ている form, and 家の電気が is what went out."}]},"scene":{"ja":"大雨・強風のお知らせ","en":"A heavy rain and wind notice","intro":"A notice at the station warns about tonight's heavy rain and strong winds. Tap each word on it.","words":[{"id":"warning","word":"警報","reading":"けいほう","gloss":"warning (official)","parts":[["警","ケイ","warn"],["報","ホウ","report"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d5_warning"},{"id":"wind","word":"強風","reading":"きょうふう","gloss":"strong wind","parts":[["強","キョウ","strong"],["風","フウ","wind"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d5_wind"},{"id":"latest","word":"最新","reading":"さいしん","gloss":"latest","parts":[["最","サイ","most: 最中"],["新","シン","new"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d5_latest"},{"id":"traffic","word":"交通","reading":"こうつう","gloss":"traffic, transport","parts":[["交","コウ","cross, mix"],["通","ツウ","pass"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d5_traffic"},{"id":"delay","word":"遅れ","reading":"おくれ","gloss":"delay","parts":[["遅","おく","late"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d5_delay"},{"id":"danger","word":"危険","reading":"きけん","gloss":"danger, dangerous","parts":[["危","キ","danger"],["険","ケン","risky"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d5_danger"},{"id":"window","word":"窓","reading":"まど","gloss":"window","parts":[["窓","まど","window"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d5_window"},{"id":"plan","word":"予定","reading":"よてい","gloss":"plan, schedule","parts":[["予","ヨ","before"],["定","テイ","fix, set"]],"clip":"s_n3u1d5_plan"}],"check":{"id":"n3u01d5.k1","kind":"choice","type":"漢字読み","label":"How the exam asks it","q":"大雨_警報_が出たので、外出はひかえてください。","options":["けいぼう","げいほう","けいほ","けいほう"],"answer":4,"explain":"警報 is けいほう: 警 is ケイ and 報 is ホウ, as in 予報 and 情報. The sound does not change to ぼう or げい, and ほう is long."}},"skill":{"kind":"listening","ja":"概要理解","en":"Gist","ask":"話の前に質問はありません。まず話を聞いて、それから質問とせんたくしを聞いて、1から4の中から最もよいものを一つえらんでください。","audio":[["N","ラジオでアナウンサーが話しています。",null],["F","ニュースをお伝えします。",null],["F","今日の午後三時ごろ、北山市で急に雨と風が強くなりました。","きょうのごごさんじごろ、きたやましできゅうにあめとかぜがつよくなりました。"],["F","雨と風が強くなったとたん、市内のあちこちで電気が消え、およそ二万けんの家でていでんしました。","あめとかぜがつよくなったとたん、しないのあちこちででんきがきえ、およそにまんけんのいえでていでんしました。"],["F","駅前などの信号も消えたため、道路はしばらく大変こみました。","えきまえなどのしんごうもきえたため、どうろはしばらくたいへんこみました。"],["F","また、電車も一時間ほど止まりましたが、今はふだんどおり動いています。","また、でんしゃもいちじかんほどとまりましたが、いまはふだんどおりうごいています。"],["F","電力会社の話では、強い風で木がたおれて、でんせんが切れたそうです。","でんりょくがいしゃのはなしでは、つよいかぜできがたおれて、でんせんがきれたそうです。"],["F","電気は夕方までにほとんどの家でもどりましたが、まだ使えない家もあり、明日の朝までには、すべての家でもどる予定です。","でんきはゆうがたまでにほとんどのいえでもどりましたが、まだつかえないいえもあり、あしたのあさまでには、すべてのいえでもどるよていです。"],["N","このニュースは、主に何について伝えていますか。","このニュースは、おもになにについてつたえていますか。"],["N","1","いち"],["N","雨が何時ごろやむか","あめがなんじごろやむか"],["N","2","に"],["N","電車が止まった理由","でんしゃがとまったりゆう"],["N","3","さん"],["N","ていでんのときに家で気をつけること","ていでんのときにいえできをつけること"],["N","4","よん"],["N","急な雨と風で起きたていでんのこと","きゅうなあめとかぜでおきたていでんのこと"]],"item":{"id":"n3u01d5.r1","kind":"choice","type":"概要理解","q":"このニュースは、主に何について伝えていますか。","script":["ナレーター：ラジオでアナウンサーが話しています。","女：ニュースをお伝えします。今日の午後三時ごろ、北山市で急に雨と風が強くなりました。雨と風が強くなったとたん、市内のあちこちで電気が消え、およそ二万けんの家でていでんしました。駅前などの信号も消えたため、道路はしばらく大変こみました。また、電車も一時間ほど止まりましたが、今はふだんどおり動いています。電力会社の話では、強い風で木がたおれて、でんせんが切れたそうです。電気は夕方までにほとんどの家でもどりましたが、まだ使えない家もあり、明日の朝までには、すべての家でもどる予定です。","ナレーター：このニュースは、主に何について伝えていますか。","ナレーター：1　雨が何時ごろやむか","ナレーター：2　電車が止まった理由","ナレーター：3　ていでんのときに家で気をつけること","ナレーター：4　急な雨と風で起きたていでんのこと"],"options":["雨が何時ごろやむか","電車が止まった理由","ていでんのときに家で気をつけること","急な雨と風で起きたていでんのこと"],"printed":false,"short":["雨がやむ時間","電車が止まった理由","ていでんのときの注意","急な雨と風でのていでん"],"answer":4,"why":["The news says when the rain and wind got strong, but never when the rain will stop.","The trains stopping is one detail, and no reason is given for it.","The news gives no advice about what to do at home.",""],"explain":"The whole report follows one event: the sudden rain and wind cut the power in about 20,000 homes, then it tells the effects (traffic lights, trains), the cause (a fallen tree cut a power line) and when power will be back.","clip":"l_n3u1d5"}}},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]},{"n":2,"ja":"動作の段階","en":"Stages of an action","days":[{"title":"〜はじめる・〜だす"},{"title":"〜つづける・〜っぱなし"},{"title":"〜かける・〜かけの"},{"title":"〜きる・〜きれない"},{"title":"〜たまま・〜ずに"},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]},{"n":3,"ja":"原因・理由","en":"Causes and reasons","days":[{"title":"〜おかげで・〜せいで"},{"title":"〜ため（に）（原因）・〜によって（原因）"},{"title":"〜ものだから・〜もの"},{"title":"〜からこそ・〜のだから"},{"title":"〜わけだ・〜わけではない"},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]},{"n":4,"ja":"判断・義務","en":"Judgements and duties","days":[{"title":"〜わけがない・〜わけにはいかない"},{"title":"〜しかない・〜ないことはない"},{"title":"〜べきだ・〜べきではない"},{"title":"〜はずだった・〜はずなのに"},{"title":"〜に違いない・〜に決まっている"},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]},{"n":5,"ja":"様子・たとえ","en":"Looks and likenesses","days":[{"title":"〜らしい（典型）・〜らしくない"},{"title":"〜っぽい・〜みたいな"},{"title":"まるで〜ようだ・〜のような"},{"title":"〜ように見える・〜ような気がする"},{"title":"〜ふりをする・〜つもりで"},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]},{"n":6,"ja":"伝聞・引用","en":"Hearsay and quoting","days":[{"title":"〜によると・〜ということだ"},{"title":"〜とのことだ・〜と言われている"},{"title":"〜って（伝聞）・〜んだって"},{"title":"〜という・〜といった"},{"title":"〜とか（伝聞）・〜っけ"},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]},{"n":7,"ja":"対象・立場","en":"Topics and viewpoints","days":[{"title":"〜について・〜に関して"},{"title":"〜に対して・〜にとって"},{"title":"〜として・〜としては"},{"title":"〜によって（ちがい）・〜によっては"},{"title":"〜向け・〜向き"},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]},{"n":8,"ja":"程度・比較","en":"Degree and comparison","days":[{"title":"〜ほど・〜くらい（程度）"},{"title":"〜ほど〜ない・〜くらい〜はない"},{"title":"〜ば〜ほど・〜につれて"},{"title":"〜に比べて・〜一方（で）"},{"title":"できるだけ〜・〜だけでなく"},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]},{"n":9,"ja":"逆接・譲歩","en":"Contrast and concession","days":[{"title":"〜くせに・〜ながら（も）"},{"title":"〜ても〜ても・たとえ〜ても"},{"title":"〜といっても・〜にしても"},{"title":"〜反面・〜けれども"},{"title":"〜わりに・〜にしては"},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]},{"n":10,"ja":"強調・限定","en":"Emphasis and limits","days":[{"title":"〜こそ・〜さえ"},{"title":"〜まで（も）・〜ばかり"},{"title":"〜てばかりいる・〜ばかりでなく"},{"title":"〜なんて・〜など（軽視）"},{"title":"〜くらい（軽視）・〜でも（例示）"},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]},{"n":11,"ja":"願い・すすめ","en":"Wishes and advice","days":[{"title":"〜ばよかった・〜たらいいのに"},{"title":"〜ように（願い）・〜ますように"},{"title":"〜ことだ（忠告）・〜ことはない"},{"title":"〜てもらいたい・〜ていただきたい"},{"title":"〜ことにしている・〜ことになっている"},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]},{"n":12,"ja":"話しことば","en":"Spoken Japanese","days":[{"title":"〜ちゃう・〜とく"},{"title":"〜てる・〜なきゃ／〜なくちゃ"},{"title":"〜じゃない（確認）・〜でしょ"},{"title":"〜なんか・〜って（話題）"},{"title":"〜かな・〜ってば"},{"title":"まとめ：似ている文法"}],"test":[]}],"items":{"n3u01d1.c1":{"id":"n3u01d1.c1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Which one takes の?","q":"父は^食事の^（　　）、この薬を飲んでいます。","options":["ごとに","たびに","おきに"],"answer":2,"why":["ごとに joins a noun directly, with no の: 食事ごとに.","An event as noun + の + たびに: every time he eats, he takes this medicine.","おきに also joins a noun directly, usually a number, as in 一日おきに."],"unit":1,"day":1,"step":"compare"},"n3u01d1.d1":{"id":"n3u01d1.d1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"この写真を^見る^（　　）、国の家族を思い出します。","options":["までに","ように","たびに","あとで"],"answer":3,"why":["までに sets a deadline. Remembering your family is not something done by a deadline.","ように gives a goal or a way of doing something. Looking at a photo is neither here.","Dictionary form + たびに: each time I look at this photo, the same thing happens.","あとで follows the た form (見たあとで), not the dictionary form."],"unit":1,"day":1,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d1.d2":{"id":"n3u01d1.d2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"引っ[越|こ]しをする（　　）、^いつも^物の多さにおどろきます。","options":["たびに","ために","までに","ように"],"answer":1,"why":["Every time I move house, I am surprised by how much stuff I have. いつも shows it happens each time.","ために with the dictionary form gives a purpose. Moving house is not done in order to be surprised.","までに sets a deadline, which does not fit a feeling.","ように gives a goal or a way of doing something. Being surprised is neither."],"unit":1,"day":1,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d1.d3":{"id":"n3u01d1.d3","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"駅前から[空港|くうこう]まで、バスが^十五分^（　　）出ています。","options":["あいだに","たびに","のに","ごとに"],"answer":4,"why":["あいだに needs の after a noun (十五分のあいだに), and it means within one stretch of time, not over and over.","たびに follows an event. 十五分 is a length of time, not an event.","のに joins two clauses with a contrast. 十五分 is a noun, and there is no contrast here.","A length of time + ごとに: a bus leaves every fifteen minutes."],"unit":1,"day":1,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d1.d4":{"id":"n3u01d1.d4","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"このホテルは、^[部屋|へや]^（　　）かべの色が[違|ちが]います。","options":["たびに","ごとに","までに","ばかりに"],"answer":2,"why":["たびに follows an event, as in とまるたびに. A room is not an event.","Noun + ごとに: each room has a different wall colour.","までに sets a deadline, and a room is not a time.","ばかりに gives a cause with a bad result, and it does not join a bare noun."],"unit":1,"day":1,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d1.d5":{"id":"n3u01d1.d5","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"この歌を","after":"思い出します。","tiles":["聞く","たびに","楽しかった","ころを"],"star":2,"bank":[2,3,0,1],"hint":"この歌を needs a verb right after it. たびに follows the dictionary form.","full":"この歌を聞く{たびに}楽しかったころを思い出します。","explain":"この歌を goes with 聞く, and たびに follows the dictionary form. 楽しかった describes ころ, and ころを is what I remember: every time I hear this song, I remember happy times.","unit":1,"day":1,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d1.d6":{"id":"n3u01d1.d6","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"このバスは","after":"時間がかかります。","tiles":["駅","ごとに","止まる","ので"],"star":2,"bank":[3,2,1,0],"hint":"ごとに joins a noun directly. ので follows a verb and gives the reason.","full":"このバスは駅{ごとに}止まるので時間がかかります。","explain":"駅ごとに (at every station) tells where the bus stops, so it comes before 止まる. ので follows 止まる and gives the reason it takes time.","unit":1,"day":1,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d1.e1":{"id":"n3u01d1.e1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"人の前で話す（　　）、きんちょうして声が小さくなってしまう。","options":["たびに","までに","ために","ように"],"answer":1,"explain":"Every time I speak in front of people, I get nervous and my voice gets quiet: dictionary form + たびに, with the same result each time. までに sets a deadline, ために gives a purpose, and ように gives a goal or a way of doing something; none of them fits a result that happens each time.","unit":1,"day":1,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d1.e2":{"id":"n3u01d1.e2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"この英語教室では、一か月（　　）席が変わります。","options":["たびに","ために","までに","ごとに"],"answer":4,"explain":"A length of time + ごとに: the seats change every month. たびに follows an event, not a length of time. ために gives a purpose or a cause, and までに sets a deadline; neither fits a change that repeats.","unit":1,"day":1,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d1.e3":{"id":"n3u01d1.e3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"姉は","after":"おみやげを買ってきてくれる。","tiles":["旅行","の","たびに","おいしい"],"star":2,"bank":[3,2,0,1],"full":"姉は旅行の{たびに}おいしいおみやげを買ってきてくれる。","explain":"旅行, の, たびに, おいしい. A noun takes の before たびに, and おいしい must sit right before おみやげ: every time she travels, my sister brings back tasty souvenirs.","unit":1,"day":1,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d1.k1":{"id":"n3u01d1.k1","kind":"choice","type":"漢字読み","label":"How the exam asks it","q":"この薬を飲むと、_眠気_が出ることがあります。","options":["みんき","ねむけ","ねむき","みんけ"],"answer":2,"explain":"眠気 is read ねむけ, drowsiness: 眠 has its kun reading ねむ (as in 眠い), and 気 becomes け, as in 寒気. みんき and みんけ use the on reading ミン, and ねむき keeps き.","unit":1,"day":1,"step":"scene"},"n3u01d1.r1":{"id":"n3u01d1.r1","kind":"choice","type":"課題理解","q":"男の人はこのあと、まず何をしますか。","script":["ナレーター：薬局で、女の人と男の人が話しています。男の人はこのあと、まず何をしますか。","女：お待たせしました。こちらが痛み止めです。八時間ごとに一つ飲んでください。","男：はい。食事のあとに飲むんですよね。","女：ええ、できれば食後にお願いします。空腹時に飲むと、おなかが痛くなることがありますので。","男：実は、歯が痛くて、朝から何も食べていないんです。すぐに飲みたいんですが。","女：でしたら、パンを少し食べてからでもだいじょうぶですよ。","男：そうですか。あ、この薬を飲むと眠くなりますか。今日は車で来ているんです。","女：飲むたびに眠くなる方もいます。飲んだあとは、運転しないでください。","男：わかりました。じゃあ、家に帰ってから、何か食べて飲みます。","女：はい。お水はお持ちですか。","男：家にあるので、だいじょうぶです。","ナレーター：男の人はこのあと、まず何をしますか。"],"options":["薬を飲む","パンを食べる","車で家に帰る","水を買う"],"printed":true,"short":["薬を飲む","パンを食べる","家に帰る","水を買う"],"answer":3,"why":["He wanted to take it at once, but he must not drive after taking it, so the medicine comes last.","The woman suggests bread, but he decides to go home first and eat there.","He came by car and must not drive after the medicine: 家に帰ってから、何か食べて飲みます. Going home comes first.","He has water at home (家にあるので), so he does not buy any."],"unit":1,"day":1,"step":"skill","clip":"l_n3u1d1"},"n3u01d2.c1":{"id":"n3u01d2.c1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Every day or every other day?","q":"父は毎日ではなく、一日（　　）ジョギングをしています。","options":["ごとに","ぶりに","おきに"],"answer":3,"why":["一日ごとに means every day, and 毎日ではなく rules that out.","ぶりに is for one event after a gap. Here jogging is a habit (しています).","Not every day but every other day: 一日おきに."],"unit":1,"day":2,"step":"compare"},"n3u01d2.d1":{"id":"n3u01d2.d1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"駅前の道には、^五十メートル^（　　）ベンチが[置|お]いてあります。","options":["ぶりに","おきに","たびに","までに"],"answer":2,"why":["ぶりに needs a length of time and one event after a gap. 五十メートル is a distance.","Distance + おきに: there is a bench every fifty metres.","たびに follows a verb or a noun with の (行くたびに), not a distance.","までに gives a deadline. 五十メートルまでに does not make sense here."],"unit":1,"day":2,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d2.d2":{"id":"n3u01d2.d2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"^先週^、五年（　　）テニスをしました。","options":["おきに","ごとに","間","ぶりに"],"answer":4,"why":["おきに is for something that repeats, but 先週 points to one game.","ごとに is also for something that repeats (every five years), not one game last week.","五年間テニスをしました says you played for five years, which does not fit 先週.","One game last week, after five years without tennis: 五年ぶりに."],"unit":1,"day":2,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d2.d3":{"id":"n3u01d2.d3","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"この薬は強いので、一日（　　）、^二日に一回^だけ飲んでください。","options":["おきに","ごとに","ぶりに","までに"],"answer":1,"why":["一日おきに skips a day: once every two days, as 二日に一回 says.","一日ごとに means every day, which is not 二日に一回.","ぶりに is for one event after a gap, not a rule for taking medicine.","一日までに would be a deadline, which does not fit 二日に一回."],"unit":1,"day":2,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d2.d4":{"id":"n3u01d2.d4","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"三年（　　）^ふるさと^は、ずいぶん[変|か]わっていました。","options":["ぶりに","おきの","ぶりの","ごとの"],"answer":3,"why":["ぶりに goes before a verb (三年ぶりに帰った). Here a noun, ふるさと, follows.","おきの is for things that come at intervals. The hometown does not.","Before a noun, ぶりの: my hometown, seen again after three years, had changed a lot.","ごとの is for things that repeat. The hometown does not."],"unit":1,"day":2,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d2.d5":{"id":"n3u01d2.d5","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"医者に、","after":"言われました。","tiles":["一日","おきに","運動する","ように"],"star":2,"bank":[2,0,3,1],"hint":"おきに follows a number + counter. ように follows a verb in the dictionary form.","full":"医者に、一日{おきに}運動するように言われました。","explain":"一日おきに is one unit, and it tells when to exercise, so it comes before 運動する. ように follows the verb and comes right before 言われました: the doctor told me to exercise every other day.","unit":1,"day":2,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d2.d6":{"id":"n3u01d2.d6","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"高校のクラス会で","after":"、少しも[変|か]わっていませんでした。","tiles":["十年","ぶりに","会った","友だちは"],"star":2,"bank":[3,1,0,2],"hint":"ぶりに follows a length of time and goes before a verb. Who had not changed?","full":"高校のクラス会で十年{ぶりに}会った友だちは、少しも[変|か]わっていませんでした。","explain":"十年ぶりに goes before the verb 会った, and 十年ぶりに会った describes 友だち. 友だちは is the topic of 変わっていませんでした, so it comes last.","unit":1,"day":2,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d2.e1":{"id":"n3u01d2.e1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"この通りには、百メートル（　　）コンビニがあります。","options":["おきに","ぶりに","たびに","あとに"],"answer":1,"explain":"Distance + おきに: there is a convenience store every hundred metres. ぶりに needs a length of time and one event after a gap, たびに follows a verb or a noun with の, and あとに does not follow a distance.","unit":1,"day":2,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d2.e2":{"id":"n3u01d2.e2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"大学を出てから一度も便りがなかった友人から、二十年（　　）手紙がとどきました。","options":["おきの","ごとの","までの","ぶりの"],"answer":4,"explain":"The friend sent nothing for twenty years, so this letter is one event after a long gap, and 手紙 is a noun: ぶりの. おきの and ごとの would mean letters came again and again, which 一度も rules out. 二十年までの手紙 does not make sense.","unit":1,"day":2,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d2.e3":{"id":"n3u01d2.e3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"仕事が落ち着いたら、","after":"、海へ行くつもりです。","tiles":["二年","ぶりの","休みを","取って"],"star":2,"bank":[1,3,0,2],"full":"仕事が落ち着いたら、二年ぶりの{休みを}取って、海へ行くつもりです。","explain":"二年, ぶりの, 休みを, 取って. 二年ぶりの describes the noun 休み, 休みを is the object of 取って, and 取って joins the next part, 海へ行く: when work calms down, I will take my first holiday in two years and go to the sea.","unit":1,"day":2,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d2.k1":{"id":"n3u01d2.k1","kind":"choice","type":"漢字読み","label":"How the exam asks it","q":"同窓会の_出欠_は、はがきで知らせてください。","options":["しゅつけつ","しゅっきつ","しゅっけつ","でけつ"],"answer":3,"explain":"出欠 is read しゅっけつ: 出 becomes しゅっ before け, and 欠 is けつ. しゅつけつ has no small っ, しゅっきつ has き instead of け, and でけつ uses the wrong reading of 出.","unit":1,"day":2,"step":"scene"},"n3u01d2.r1":{"id":"n3u01d2.r1","kind":"choice","type":"読解・内容理解（短文）","q":"このメールを読んだ人がしなければならないことは何か。","options":["十月三十一日までに、会費を払う。","来られるかどうかを、十月三十一日までにメールで知らせる。","一年おきに集まれるかどうか、返事をする。","来られない場合は、田中先生にそのことを伝える。"],"short":["会費を払う","出欠をメールで知らせる","一年おきに集まれるか返事する","田中先生に伝える"],"answer":2,"explain":"The request is 出欠は、十月三十一日までに、このメールに返信して知らせてください: everyone replies by email, by 31 October, to say whether they can come.","why":["The fee is paid on the day, at the reception desk (当日、受付で).","","Meeting every other year is only Yamada's hope (集まれたらいいな). Nobody is asked to answer it.","Teacher Tanaka is coming, but people who cannot come reply to this email, not to him."],"unit":1,"day":2,"step":"skill"},"n3u01d3.c1":{"id":"n3u01d3.c1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"仕事のあとで","q":"店を[閉|し]めて（　　）、みんなで食事に行きましょう。","options":["以来","はじめて","から"],"answer":3,"why":["以来 needs a state or habit that has gone on since then, and it cannot lead to an invitation like 行きましょう.","はじめて needs a new understanding or ability after it, not an invitation.","One action after another: close the shop, then go and eat. てから fits plans and invitations."],"unit":1,"day":3,"step":"compare"},"n3u01d3.d1":{"id":"n3u01d3.d1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"[彼|かれ]は二年前に[転職|てんしょく]（　　）、^ずっと^毎日楽しそうに働いています。","options":["するたびに","して以来","するために","してはじめて"],"answer":2,"why":["たびに is for every time something happens. 二年前に points to one event, not a repeated one.","One past event, and a state that has gone on since then: ずっと…働いています.","ために gives a purpose. Changing jobs is not the purpose of working happily.","はじめて needs a new understanding or ability after it. ずっと…ています describes a lasting state instead."],"unit":1,"day":3,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d3.d2":{"id":"n3u01d3.d2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"^仕事を[失|うしな]って^（　　）、毎日働けることのありがたさが分かりました。","options":["以来","もらって","はじめて","おいて"],"answer":3,"why":["以来 needs a state or habit that has gone on since then. 分かりました here is one moment of understanding.","てもらう means someone does something for you. Nobody lost a job for the speaker.","Only after losing the job did the speaker understand: てはじめて + 分かりました.","ておく is for doing something in advance on purpose. Nobody loses a job to get ready for something."],"unit":1,"day":3,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d3.d3":{"id":"n3u01d3.d3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"[祖母|そぼ]は","after":"あまり出なくなりました。","tiles":["足を","[痛|いた]めて","以来","外に"],"star":1,"bank":[3,2,0,1],"hint":"以来 follows the te-form. What did she hurt, and where does she not go any more?","full":"[祖母|そぼ]は足を[痛|いた]めて{以来}外にあまり出なくなりました。","explain":"足を goes with 痛めて, and 以来 follows the te-form. 外に goes with 出なくなりました: since she hurt her leg, she has hardly gone out.","unit":1,"day":3,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d3.d4":{"id":"n3u01d3.d4","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"会社に着いて（　　）、^すぐに^[部長|ぶちょう]に[呼|よ]ばれました。","options":["から","以来","はじめて","ばかりで"],"answer":1,"why":["One event right after another: てから. すぐに shows it happened straight after arriving.","以来 needs something that has gone on until now. Being called once is a single event.","はじめて needs a new understanding or ability after it. Being called by the manager is neither.","てばかり means doing only one thing again and again, which does not fit 着く. \"Had just arrived\" would be 着いたばかりで."],"unit":1,"day":3,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d3.d5":{"id":"n3u01d3.d5","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"^自分で家事をして^（　　）、母の[苦労|くろう]が分かりました。","options":["も","以来","もらって","はじめて"],"answer":4,"why":["ても means even if or even though. Doing the housework is the reason the speaker understands, not something against it.","以来 needs a state or habit that has gone on since then. 分かりました is one moment of understanding.","てもらう means someone else does it for you, but 自分で says the speaker did it.","Only after doing the housework herself did the speaker understand: てはじめて + 分かりました."],"unit":1,"day":3,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d3.d6":{"id":"n3u01d3.d6","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"[実際|じっさい]に店で","after":"分かるようになりました。","tiles":["働いて","はじめて","お[客|きゃく]さんの","気持ちが"],"star":2,"bank":[2,0,3,1],"hint":"はじめて follows the te-form. Whose feelings did the speaker come to understand?","full":"[実際|じっさい]に店で働いて{はじめて}お[客|きゃく]さんの気持ちが分かるようになりました。","explain":"店で goes with 働いて, and はじめて follows the te-form. お客さんの describes 気持ちが, which goes with 分かるようになりました.","unit":1,"day":3,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d3.e1":{"id":"n3u01d3.e1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"この店は十年前に（　　）、ずっと同じ味を守っています。","options":["開店するたびに","開店して以来","開店してはじめて","開店したばかりで"],"answer":2,"explain":"One past event (十年前に) and a state that has gone on since then (ずっと…守っています): して以来. たびに needs a repeated event, はじめて needs a new understanding after it, and ばかり (just opened) does not fit ten years ago.","unit":1,"day":3,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d3.e2":{"id":"n3u01d3.e2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"社会に出て（　　）、学生時代がどんなに楽だったかが分かった。","options":["はじめて","以来","おいて","ばかりで"],"answer":1,"explain":"Only after starting work did the speaker realise how easy student life was: てはじめて + 分かった. 以来 needs a state that has gone on, not one moment of understanding. ておく is for preparing in advance, and 出てばかりで does not make sense here.","unit":1,"day":3,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d3.e3":{"id":"n3u01d3.e3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"二人は","after":"親しくしています。","tiles":["二十年前に","知り合って","以来","ずっと"],"star":1,"bank":[3,0,2,1],"full":"二人は二十年前に{知り合って}以来ずっと親しくしています。","explain":"二十年前に, 知り合って, 以来, ずっと. 二十年前に goes with 知り合って, 以来 follows the te-form, and ずっと goes with the lasting state 親しくしています.","unit":1,"day":3,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d3.k1":{"id":"n3u01d3.k1","kind":"choice","type":"漢字読み","label":"How the exam asks it","q":"このパンは週末_限定_です。","options":["けんてい","げんじょう","かんてい","げんてい"],"answer":4,"explain":"限定 is read げんてい: this bread is sold only at the weekend. けんてい has け instead of げ, げんじょう is a different word (現状, the present state), and かんてい reads 限 as かん.","unit":1,"day":3,"step":"scene"},"n3u01d3.r1":{"id":"n3u01d3.r1","kind":"choice","type":"ポイント理解","q":"男の人は、どうしてパン屋を始めましたか。","script":["ナレーター：パン屋で、女の人と店の男の人が話しています。男の人は、どうしてパン屋を始めましたか。","女：開店三十年、おめでとうございます。","男：ありがとうございます。店を開いて以来、毎朝四時に起きてパンを作っています。","女：子どものころから、パン屋さんになりたかったんですか。","男：いいえ。前は会社員で、パンにはあまりきょうみがなかったんです。","女：え、そうなんですか。じゃあ、会社のお仕事が大変だったとか…。","男：いえ、仕事は忙しかったですが、楽しかったですよ。ただ、仕事でフランスに行ったとき、小さな店でパンを食べたんです。それを食べてはじめて、本当においしいパンがどんなものか分かりました。それで、自分でも作りたくなったんです。","女：ご家族は賛成してくださいましたか。","男：いえ、妻には反対されましたよ。でも、今はいっしょに店をやっています。","ナレーター：男の人は、どうしてパン屋を始めましたか。"],"options":["会社の仕事が大変だったから","フランスで食べたパンがおいしかったから","家族にすすめられたから","子どものころからパン屋になりたかったから"],"printed":true,"short":["仕事が大変","フランスのパン","家族のすすめ","子どものころの夢"],"answer":2,"why":["He says his job was busy but fun: 忙しかったですが、楽しかったですよ.","Only after eating that bread in France did he understand what really good bread is (食べてはじめて…分かりました), and then he wanted to make it himself.","His family did not suggest it. His wife was against it at first: 妻には反対されました.","He says no: he was an office worker and not very interested in bread."],"unit":1,"day":3,"step":"skill","clip":"l_n3u1d3"},"n3u01d4.c1":{"id":"n3u01d4.c1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Which ところ?","q":"ゲームで[遊|あそ]んでいる（　　）、父に見られてしまいました。","options":["ところに","ところを","ところです"],"answer":2,"why":["ところに is followed by something that arrives or happens. 見られる needs the scene as its object, so を.","Father saw the scene: ところを ＋ 見られる.","ところです ends a sentence. It cannot join the next clause with a comma."],"unit":1,"day":4,"step":"compare"},"n3u01d4.d1":{"id":"n3u01d4.d1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"[部屋|へや]をそうじしている（　　）、^友だちが急に[遊|あそ]びに来ました^。","options":["ところを","たびに","ところに","ところだ"],"answer":3,"why":["ところを needs a verb like 見る or 見つかる after it. 友だちが来る does not take it as an object.","たびに means every time and follows the dictionary form. Here it is one visit that came out of the blue (急に).","In the middle of cleaning, a friend arrived: ている ＋ ところに.","ところだ ends a sentence, so it cannot join the next clause."],"unit":1,"day":4,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d4.d2":{"id":"n3u01d4.d2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"電車の中で[寝|ね]ている（　　）、友だちに^写真をとられて^しまいました。","options":["ところに","ところを","たびに","[以来|いらい]"],"answer":2,"why":["写真をとられる needs the scene as its object. ところに would need someone arriving, as in 友だちが来た.","The friend photographed the scene of me sleeping: ところを ＋ とられる.","たびに follows the dictionary form and means every time. This is one event.","以来 follows the て form (寝て以来) and means ever since. It does not fit here."],"unit":1,"day":4,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d4.d3":{"id":"n3u01d4.d3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"ちょうどシャワーを","after":"人が来ました。","tiles":["あびて","いる","ところへ","[宅配便|たくはいびん]の"],"star":3,"bank":[2,3,0,1],"hint":"シャワーを takes a verb. Which tile describes 人?","full":"ちょうどシャワーをあびているところへ[宅配便|たくはいびん]の人が来ました。","explain":"シャワーをあびている is what I was doing. ところへ comes after it, and the person who arrived follows: 宅配便の人が来ました.","unit":1,"day":4,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d4.d4":{"id":"n3u01d4.d4","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"お[忙|いそが]しい（　　）、^[資料|しりょう]を見ていただいて^ありがとうございました。","options":["たびに","うちに","ところだ","ところを"],"answer":4,"why":["たびに means every time, and it does not follow お忙しい. This is a thank-you for one favour.","うちに means before a change comes. Here the speaker thanks someone; nothing is about to change.","ところだ ends a sentence, so it cannot join the thanks that follows.","The set phrase of thanks: お忙しいところを ＋ 〜ていただいて, ありがとうございました."],"unit":1,"day":4,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d4.d5":{"id":"n3u01d4.d5","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"すみません、今から^[会議|かいぎ]が始まる^（　　）。あとでこちらから電話します。","options":["ところなんです","ところに","ところを","たびに"],"answer":1,"why":["Dictionary form ＋ ところだ: the meeting is about to start. なんです explains why the speaker cannot talk now.","ところに needs a clause after it in the same sentence. Here the sentence ends.","ところを also needs a verb after it, such as 見られる. Here the sentence ends.","たびに means every time, and it also needs a clause after it."],"unit":1,"day":4,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d4.d6":{"id":"n3u01d4.d6","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"お休みの","after":"、ありがとうございました。","tiles":["ところを","わざわざ","来て","いただき"],"star":1,"bank":[3,1,0,2],"hint":"お休みの needs a noun right after it. Where does わざわざ (taking the trouble) go?","full":"お休みのところをわざわざ来ていただき、ありがとうございました。","explain":"お休みのところを is the set phrase. わざわざ comes before the verb it describes, and 来ていただき joins the thanks.","unit":1,"day":4,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d4.e1":{"id":"n3u01d4.e1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"夕飯を作っている（　　）、となりの人が野菜を持ってきてくれた。","options":["ところに","ところを","たびに","ところだ"],"answer":1,"explain":"In the middle of cooking, the neighbour arrived with vegetables: ている ＋ ところに. ところを needs a verb like 見る after it, たびに follows the dictionary form and means every time, and ところだ ends a sentence.","unit":1,"day":4,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d4.e2":{"id":"n3u01d4.e2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"弟はれいぞうこのケーキをこっそり食べている（　　）、母に見つかってしまった。","options":["ところに","ごとに","ところを","以来"],"answer":3,"explain":"見つかる takes the scene as its object: 食べているところを見つかった. ところに would need someone arriving, as in 母が来た. ごとに follows a noun or the dictionary form, and 以来 follows the て form.","unit":1,"day":4,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d4.e3":{"id":"n3u01d4.e3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"アルバイト中にゲームを","after":"見つかってしまった。","tiles":["して","いる","ところを","店長に"],"star":2,"bank":[3,2,0,1],"full":"アルバイト中にゲームをしている{ところを}店長に見つかってしまった。","explain":"して, いる, ところを, 店長に. ゲームをしている is the scene, ところを makes it the thing found, and 店長に shows who found it.","unit":1,"day":4,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d4.k1":{"id":"n3u01d4.k1","kind":"choice","type":"漢字読み","label":"How the exam asks it","q":"_不在_の間に、お客様から電話がありました。","options":["ぶざい","ふさい","ふざい","ふうざい"],"answer":3,"explain":"不在 is read ふざい: while you were out, a customer phoned. ぶざい uses the ぶ of 不用心, which is not this word, ふさい has さ instead of ざ, and ふうざい adds a long う.","unit":1,"day":4,"step":"scene"},"n3u01d4.r1":{"id":"n3u01d4.r1","kind":"choice","type":"読解・内容理解（中文）","q":"この手紙の内容に合うものはどれか。","options":["引っ越しの日、山田さんが来る前ににもつを全部運んでいた。","山田さんがおさらを割ったところを見て、恥ずかしく思った。","山田さんに手伝ってもらったので、その日の夕方には運び終わった。","来月、山田さんの家へ食事に行くことになっている。"],"short":["山田さんが来る前に運んでいた","山田さんが割ったのを見た","手伝ってもらい夕方に運び終わった","山田さんの家へ食事に行く"],"answer":3,"explain":"困っているところに山田さんが来てくださって and おかげで、夕方には全部運び終わりました: with Yamada's help the moving was done by evening.","why":["The writer thought she could not finish alone, and was still struggling when Yamada arrived (困っているところに).","It is the other way round. The writer broke the plate, and Yamada saw it (ところを山田さんに見られて).","","The writer invites Yamada to her own new place (食事に来てください), not the other way round."],"unit":1,"day":4,"step":"skill"},"n3u01d5.c1":{"id":"n3u01d5.c1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Which one takes an invitation?","q":"仕事が（　　）、飲みに行きましょう。","options":["終わる[最中|さいちゅう]に","終わったとたん","終わったらすぐ"],"answer":3,"why":["[最中|さいちゅう] joins a noun with の or the ている form. Also, 終わる is over in a moment, so it has no middle.","行きましょう is an invitation, and an invitation cannot follow とたん.","たらすぐ can take an invitation: as soon as work is over, let's go for a drink."],"unit":1,"day":5,"step":"compare"},"n3u01d5.d1":{"id":"n3u01d5.d1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"大事な電話をしている（　　）、^となりの[部屋|へや]から大きな音がしました^。","options":["とたんに","[最中|さいちゅう]に","あとで","ところを"],"answer":2,"why":["とたんに follows the た form, as in 電話をしたとたんに. Here the verb is している.","ている + [最中|さいちゅう]に: right in the middle of the call, a loud noise broke in.","あとで follows the た form or a noun with の, not the ている form.","ところを needs a verb after it that acts on the person in that scene, such as 見られる or じゃまする. 音がしました is not one."],"unit":1,"day":5,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d5.d2":{"id":"n3u01d5.d2","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"わたしが","after":"、家中の電気が[消|き]えました。","tiles":["ドライヤーの","スイッチを","入れた","とたん"],"star":2,"bank":[2,3,1,0],"hint":"とたん follows the た form. What did the speaker turn on, and the switch of what?","full":"わたしがドライヤーのスイッチを入れた{とたん}、家中の電気が[消|き]えました。","explain":"ドライヤーの describes スイッチ, and スイッチを is what 入れた takes. とたん comes right after the た form 入れた: the moment I switched on the hair dryer, every light in the house went out.","unit":1,"day":5,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d5.d3":{"id":"n3u01d5.d3","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose what follows","q":"げんかんのドアを開けた^とたん^、（　　）。","options":["中に入ってください","中に入りましょう","ねこが外に[飛|と]び出しました","中に入ろうと思います"],"answer":3,"why":["This is a request, and a request cannot follow とたん.","This is an invitation, and an invitation cannot follow とたん.","Something the speaker did not plan happened at once: the cat shot out of the door.","This is the speaker's own plan (〜ようと思います), which cannot follow とたん."],"unit":1,"day":5,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d5.d4":{"id":"n3u01d5.d4","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"すみません、^今は食事の^（　　）なので、あとでこちらから電話します。","options":["[最中|さいちゅう]","とたん","たび","ごと"],"answer":1,"why":["Noun + の + [最中|さいちゅう] at the end of a clause: I am in the middle of a meal right now.","とたん follows the た form of a verb, not a noun with の.","たび means every time. It takes に and a repeated event after it; it does not say what is going on now.","ごと joins a noun directly, without の (一日ごと), and means every."],"unit":1,"day":5,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d5.d5":{"id":"n3u01d5.d5","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"子どもは^母親の[顔|かお]を見た^（　　）、なき出しました。","options":["[最中|さいちゅう]に","うちに","まえに","とたん"],"answer":4,"why":["[最中|さいちゅう] needs a noun with の or the ている form. 見た is the た form.","うちに follows the ている form or the dictionary form, not the た form.","まえに follows the dictionary form: 見るまえに.","た form + とたん: the moment the child saw his mother's face, he burst into tears."],"unit":1,"day":5,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d5.d6":{"id":"n3u01d5.d6","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"社長が","after":"、だれかのスマホが[鳴|な]りました。","tiles":["新しい","計画を","説明している","[最中|さいちゅう]に"],"star":1,"bank":[2,0,3,1],"hint":"[最中|さいちゅう] follows the ている form. What is the president explaining?","full":"社長が新しい計画を説明している{[最中|さいちゅう]に}、だれかのスマホが[鳴|な]りました。","explain":"新しい describes 計画, and 計画を is what 説明している takes. [最中|さいちゅう]に comes right after the ている form: right in the middle of the president's talk, someone's phone rang.","unit":1,"day":5,"step":"drill"},"n3u01d5.e1":{"id":"n3u01d5.e1","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"サッカーの試合の（　　）、急に強い雨が降ってきました。","options":["とたんに","うえに","最中に","ところに"],"answer":3,"explain":"Noun + の + 最中に: right in the middle of the match, heavy rain started. とたんに follows the た form of a verb, not a noun with の. 試合のうえに and 試合のところに would mean on top of the match and at the match's place, which make no sense here.","unit":1,"day":5,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d5.e2":{"id":"n3u01d5.e2","kind":"choice","type":"文の文法1","label":"Choose the form","q":"家に着いた（　　）、雨が強く降ってきました。","options":["最中に","うちに","までに","とたん"],"answer":4,"explain":"着いた is the た form, and the rain started at that very moment: とたん. 最中に needs a noun with の or the ている form. うちに and までに do not follow the た form.","unit":1,"day":5,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d5.e3":{"id":"n3u01d5.e3","kind":"star","type":"文の文法2","label":"Build the sentence","before":"ドライヤーで","after":"消えてしまいました。","tiles":["かみを","かわかしている","最中に","家の電気が"],"star":1,"bank":[3,1,0,2],"full":"ドライヤーでかみを{かわかしている}最中に家の電気が消えてしまいました。","explain":"かみを, かわかしている, 最中に, 家の電気が. かみを goes with かわかしている, 最中に follows the ている form, and 家の電気が is what went out.","unit":1,"day":5,"step":"exam"},"n3u01d5.k1":{"id":"n3u01d5.k1","kind":"choice","type":"漢字読み","label":"How the exam asks it","q":"大雨_警報_が出たので、外出はひかえてください。","options":["けいぼう","げいほう","けいほ","けいほう"],"answer":4,"explain":"警報 is けいほう: 警 is ケイ and 報 is ホウ, as in 予報 and 情報. The sound does not change to ぼう or げい, and ほう is long.","unit":1,"day":5,"step":"scene"},"n3u01d5.r1":{"id":"n3u01d5.r1","kind":"choice","type":"概要理解","q":"このニュースは、主に何について伝えていますか。","script":["ナレーター：ラジオでアナウンサーが話しています。","女：ニュースをお伝えします。今日の午後三時ごろ、北山市で急に雨と風が強くなりました。雨と風が強くなったとたん、市内のあちこちで電気が消え、およそ二万けんの家でていでんしました。駅前などの信号も消えたため、道路はしばらく大変こみました。また、電車も一時間ほど止まりましたが、今はふだんどおり動いています。電力会社の話では、強い風で木がたおれて、でんせんが切れたそうです。電気は夕方までにほとんどの家でもどりましたが、まだ使えない家もあり、明日の朝までには、すべての家でもどる予定です。","ナレーター：このニュースは、主に何について伝えていますか。","ナレーター：1　雨が何時ごろやむか","ナレーター：2　電車が止まった理由","ナレーター：3　ていでんのときに家で気をつけること","ナレーター：4　急な雨と風で起きたていでんのこと"],"options":["雨が何時ごろやむか","電車が止まった理由","ていでんのときに家で気をつけること","急な雨と風で起きたていでんのこと"],"printed":false,"short":["雨がやむ時間","電車が止まった理由","ていでんのときの注意","急な雨と風でのていでん"],"answer":4,"why":["The news says when the rain and wind got strong, but never when the rain will stop.","The trains stopping is one detail, and no reason is given for it.","The news gives no advice about what to do at home.",""],"explain":"The whole report follows one event: the sudden rain and wind cut the power in about 20,000 homes, then it tells the effects (traffic lights, trains), the cause (a fallen tree cut a power line) and when power will be back.","unit":1,"day":5,"step":"skill","clip":"l_n3u1d5"}}};
